```c
static int next(struct lexer *lexer)
{
    if (lexer->pos >= lexer->end) {
        lexer->pos = lexer->end + 1;
        return '\0';
    }
    ...
}
```

So when `pos >= end`, `next()` returns `'\0'` and the loop exits. But `strncmp` is called BEFORE `next()`. So the last `strncmp` call happens when `pos = end - 1` (or earlier).

Actually wait, let me re-trace. The loop is:
```c
